.TITLE "pbpaste"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Pastes data from the clipboard to standard output. It retrieves the current contents of the system __pasteboard__ and writes it to the terminal or redirects it to a file.

.DIV "TLDR"
**pbpaste**
Prints the current contents of the clipboard directly to the terminal.
> 

**pbpaste > file.txt**
Writes the contents of the clipboard into a specific file.
> __>__ output redirection | __file.txt__ the destination file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Combine __pbpaste__ with tools like __grep__ or __sed__ to process clipboard data directly in the terminal. It is the logical counterpart to the __pbcopy__ tool.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:pbcopy**

